{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-eigenvalue-product-expansion","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:eigenvalue-product-expansion","kind":"proposition","title":"Eigenvalue product expansion of the nuclear braid Markov trace","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-universal-braid-branching"],"tags":["eigenvalue-product","markov-trace","symmetric-channel","isospin","crossing-number","q-integer"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.eigenvalue_product_expansion","text":"eigenvalue-product-expansion.md","leanSource":"eigenvalue-product-expansion.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:eigenvalue-product-expansion\"></a><p><em>For a nucleus with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Z</code> protons and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N</code> neutrons (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A = Z + N</code>), the symmetric channel eigenvalue product of the nuclear braid in the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[2{,}1]</code> representation of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_3(R, q)</code> is:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\Lambda_{\\mathrm{sym}}\n  = q^{(Z-N)(A-1)/2} \\cdot \\Bigl(\\frac{[2]_q}{2}\\Bigr)^{\\!ZN}</code></pre>\n<p><em>Its logarithm expands in the isospin variable <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T = |Z - N|/2</code> as:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\ln|\\Lambda_{\\mathrm{sym}}|\n  = \\ell_2 \\cdot \\frac{A^2}{4}\n  \\;+\\; \\ell \\cdot T \\cdot A\n  \\;-\\; \\ell \\cdot T\n  \\;-\\; \\ell_2 \\cdot T^2</code></pre>\n<p><em>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ell = \\ln q</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ell_2 = \\ln([2]_q/2)</code>.</em></p>\n<p>The four terms correspond respectively to the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">pn</code> crossing count, the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">pp</code> vs <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">nn</code> crossing excess, a linear isospin correction, and a quadratic isospin term. The Coulomb correction arises separately from the standard channel.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/eigenvalue-product-expansion.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.5.6","page":"b/prop-eigenvalue-product-expansion","qa":{"counts":{"pass":88,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":12,"unknown":0,"stale":75},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.eigenvalue_product_expansion","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/eigenvalue-product-expansion.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
